# Docker build-context exclusions for infra/docker/Dockerfile.enclave.
#
# The enclave image only needs: enclave/, packages/, root package.json +
# yarn.lock + tsconfig.base.json + .yarnrc.yml, infra/docker/vendor/,
# infra/enclave-config/, infra/enclave-artefacts/, infra/docker/Dockerfile.*.
# Everything else bloats the context, sometimes catastrophically —
# calypso-enclave.eif alone is ~1.6 GB.

# VCS metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Top-level workspaces not used by the enclave build
apps
server
scripts
docs
de-risk

# Node / Yarn artifacts (we rebuild inside the Dockerfile)
node_modules
**/node_modules
.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz
.yarn/unplugged

# Build outputs
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.eif

# Editor / OS noise
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# Log files
*.log
**/*.log

# Vendor manifest gets consumed via the vendor/ dir itself; the .sha256
# file sits next to it but isn't referenced by the Dockerfile
# (the script reads it, not the image).
infra/docker/VENDOR-MANIFEST.sha256

# Provider-key ciphertext blob (Chunk 12) — host-served via
# infra/host/keys-broker.py. Never bake into the EIF.
infra/enclave-config/

# Environment variable files — prevent developer plaintext keys from
# accidentally baking into the image via any COPY directive.
.env
.env.*
